.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_unset_func(bc_client_t *c, const char *name);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a shell function from the bash\-server session associated with
the client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
After a successful call, the function no longer exists in the
session\(cqs function namespace.
.PP
The function sends an \f[CR]unset\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqfunc\(dq\f[R] and the given function name.
The server performs the equivalent of \f[CR]unset \-f name\f[R] in the
shell session.
.PP
If the function does not exist, the server treats this as a successful
operation (no error is returned).
This matches the behavior of \f[CR]unset \-f\f[R] in bash, which
succeeds silently when the target function is not defined.
