.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Unsetting a nonexistent function is not an error.
This matches POSIX \f[CR]unset \-f\f[R] semantics.
.IP \(bu 2
There is no \f[CR]bc_state_set_func()\f[R] function.
To define shell functions, use \f[CR]bc_eval()\f[R] with the function
definition syntax.
.IP \(bu 2
Functions marked readonly with \f[CR]readonly \-f\f[R] cannot be unset.
This restriction is enforced by the server, which returns an error
message.
.IP \(bu 2
After unsetting a function, any aliases, variables, or traps with the
same name are unaffected.
Each namespace is independent.
.IP \(bu 2
The function uses the v2 binary protocol internally.
The STATE channel request includes \f[CR]\(dqop\(dq: \(dqunset\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqns\(dq: \(dqfunc\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqname\(dq\f[R] fields.
.IP \(bu 2
A single \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R] must not be used concurrently from
multiple threads.
